      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The reports that contain cost estimates will be published; only that subgroup is selected." data-hint="The archive contains reports with and without cost estimates, so the clause must identify a subset." data-fix="The reports that contain cost estimates will be published."><p class="quiz-question">5. The archive has 20 reports, and only six contain cost estimates. Which sentence selects the six?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The reports that contain cost estimates will be published; only that subgroup is selected.">The reports that contain cost estimates will be published; only that subgroup is selected.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The reports, which contain cost estimates, will be published; the commas select only six from the archive.">The reports, which contain cost estimates, will be published; the commas select only six from the archive.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The reports, that contain cost estimates will be published.">The reports, that contain cost estimates will be published.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The final schedule, which the board approved on May 14, is online; the schedule is already uniquely identified." data-hint="Final plus the shared project context identifies one schedule before the approval detail." data-fix="The final schedule, which the board approved on May 14, is online."><p class="quiz-question">6. The project has one agreed final schedule. Which sentence adds its approval date parenthetically?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final schedule, which the board approved on May 14, is online; the schedule is already uniquely identified.">The final schedule, which the board approved on May 14, is online; the schedule is already uniquely identified.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final schedule which the board approved on May 14 is online; final never identifies a document in context.">The final schedule which the board approved on May 14 is online; final never identifies a document in context.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final schedule, the board approved it on May 14, is online.">The final schedule, the board approved it on May 14, is online.</button></div></div>
