      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Dana Ruiz, who I spoke with yesterday, will attend." data-hint="The prompt requests ordinary conversational U.S. English with the preposition at the end." data-fix="Dana Ruiz, who I spoke with yesterday, will attend."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which version naturally uses conversational preposition stranding?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, who I spoke with yesterday, will attend.">Dana Ruiz, who I spoke with yesterday, will attend.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with who I spoke with yesterday, will attend.">Dana Ruiz, with who I spoke with yesterday, will attend.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, that I spoke yesterday with, will attend.">Dana Ruiz, that I spoke yesterday with, will attend.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Dana Ruiz, with whom I spoke yesterday, will attend." data-hint="The prompt requests formal fronting, so put with before object whom and do not repeat it." data-fix="Dana Ruiz, with whom I spoke yesterday, will attend."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which version is the formal fronted equivalent?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with whom I spoke yesterday, will attend.">Dana Ruiz, with whom I spoke yesterday, will attend.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with who I spoke with yesterday, will attend.">Dana Ruiz, with who I spoke with yesterday, will attend.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, whom I spoke yesterday, will attend.">Dana Ruiz, whom I spoke yesterday, will attend.</button></div></div>
