  <h2>Let <span class="ex">which</span> comment on a whole proposition</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A comma plus <span class="ex">which</span> can refer to an entire preceding proposition: <span class="ex">The board moved the opening to September 9, which gave the team one more week.</span> The cause of the extra week is the whole decision. Whole-clause <span class="ex">which</span> commonly introduces an evaluation, consequence, or reformulation: <span class="ex">which was unexpected</span>, <span class="ex">which means...</span>, <span class="ex">which is why...</span>.</p>
  <p>Attachment must be clear. In <span class="ex">The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete</span>, a reader may hesitate between <span class="ex">budget</span>, the discussion, and even the nearby time phrase. Rewrite the intended relationship: <span class="ex">The team discussed the incomplete budget in May</span> or <span class="ex">The team discussed the budget in May. That discussion was incomplete.</span></p>
  <p>A parenthetical clause can also make a claim feel settled or backgrounded. <span class="ex">Jordan Lee, whose late review caused the delay, apologized</span> asserts a cause as background information. If the source only alleges that cause, attribute it in a main clause: <span class="ex">A newsletter alleged that the late review caused the delay, but the project file does not establish that cause.</span> Punctuation does not turn an allegation into fact.</p>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You linked whole propositions to a reaction, consequence, inference, and reason, repaired two unclear attachments, and kept an unsupported cause out of background information.">
    <h3>Whole-clause connection: make the intended source recoverable</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The board unexpectedly approved all four access changes, which was a surprise to the budget office." data-hint="Singular was points back to the complete approval event; the plural changes alone would require were." data-fix="The board unexpectedly approved all four access changes, which was a surprise to the budget office."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence clearly presents a reaction to the whole approval event rather than to the plural changes as objects?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The board unexpectedly approved all four access changes, which was a surprise to the budget office.">The board unexpectedly approved all four access changes, which was a surprise to the budget office.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The board approved all four access changes, that was a surprise to the budget office.">The board approved all four access changes, that was a surprise to the budget office.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The board, which approved, all four access changes was the budget office.">The board, which approved, all four access changes was the budget office.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the finishing team one more week." data-hint="The extra week results from the whole schedule change." data-fix="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the finishing team one more week."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence makes the consequence of the scheduling decision clear?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the finishing team one more week.">The opening moved to September 9, which gave the finishing team one more week.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The opening, that moved to September 9 gave, the team one more week.">The opening, that moved to September 9 gave, the team one more week.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="September 9 who gave the team one more week moved the opening.">September 9 who gave the team one more week moved the opening.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The west entrance will remain closed, which means visitors must use the east entrance." data-hint="Which means reformulates the practical consequence of the whole closure statement." data-fix="The west entrance will remain closed, which means visitors must use the east entrance."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence draws a practical inference from the closure?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The west entrance will remain closed, which means visitors must use the east entrance.">The west entrance will remain closed, which means visitors must use the east entrance.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The west entrance will remain closed, that means visitors use east.">The west entrance will remain closed, that means visitors use east.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The west entrance, which visitors must use the east entrance, remains closed.">The west entrance, which visitors must use the east entrance, remains closed.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The archive rooms contain rare materials, which is why they will remain closed through October." data-hint="Which is why links the whole rare-materials fact to the stated closure reason." data-fix="The archive rooms contain rare materials, which is why they will remain closed through October."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence clearly presents the rare materials as the reason for the later reopening?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The archive rooms contain rare materials, which is why they will remain closed through October.">The archive rooms contain rare materials, which is why they will remain closed through October.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The archive rooms, why contain rare materials, will remain closed through October.">The archive rooms, why contain rare materials, will remain closed through October.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The archive rooms contain rare materials, that is why they will remain closed through October.">The archive rooms contain rare materials, that is why they will remain closed through October.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The team discussed the incomplete budget in May." data-hint="Place incomplete directly before budget when the budget, not the discussion, was incomplete." data-fix="The team discussed the incomplete budget in May."><p class="quiz-question">5. The budget lacked two cost estimates, but the discussion itself was complete. Which revision removes the attachment ambiguity?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team discussed the incomplete budget in May.">The team discussed the incomplete budget in May.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete.">The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team, which was incomplete, discussed the budget in May.">The team, which was incomplete, discussed the budget in May.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The team discussed the budget in May. That discussion did not cover staffing." data-hint="Use a new sentence with an explicit noun when the whole discussion, not the budget, was incomplete." data-fix="The team discussed the budget in May. That discussion did not cover staffing."><p class="quiz-question">6. The budget document was complete, but the discussion omitted staffing. Which revision makes that scope explicit?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team discussed the budget in May. That discussion did not cover staffing.">The team discussed the budget in May. That discussion did not cover staffing.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team discussed the incomplete budget in May.">The team discussed the incomplete budget in May.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete.">The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A newsletter alleged that the late design review caused the delay, but the project file does not establish that cause." data-hint="Attribute the disputed causal claim and state the documentary limit in main clauses." data-fix="A newsletter alleged that the late design review caused the delay, but the project file does not establish that cause."><p class="quiz-question">7. The only causal claim comes from a neighborhood newsletter. Which sentence reports it without backgrounding it as fact?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A newsletter alleged that the late design review caused the delay, but the project file does not establish that cause.">A newsletter alleged that the late design review caused the delay, but the project file does not establish that cause.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Jordan Lee, whose late review caused the delay, is responsible for the entire schedule change.">Jordan Lee, whose late review caused the delay, is responsible for the entire schedule change.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The delay, which proves Jordan caused it, requires no source.">The delay, which proves Jordan caused it, requires no source.</button></div></div>
