      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The rooms that contain rare materials will remain closed">The rooms that contain rare materials will remain closed</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Jordan Lee, who presented the plan, answered questions">Jordan Lee, who presented the plan, answered questions</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The library is being renovated">The library is being renovated</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The selected advisers, all of whom attended both sessions, supported the plan">The selected advisers, all of whom attended both sessions, supported the plan</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Mark both sides of a parenthetical clause inside the main sentence: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The library, which opened in 1986, is being renovated" data-hint="Open the insertion after library and close it before the main verb is." data-fix="The library, which opened in 1986, is being renovated." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The whole-clause consequence comes at the end, so use one boundary before <span class="ex">which</span>: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the team one more week" data-hint="The main clause comes first, followed by one ending comment." data-fix="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the team one more week." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The archive has several rooms, and only some contain rare materials. Keep the identifying clause integrated: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The rooms that contain rare materials will remain closed" data-hint="No commas belong around a clause that selects the intended rooms." data-fix="The rooms that contain rare materials will remain closed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
