  <h2>Read a project file with reference and evidence intact</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Alder Street Library renovation file</h3>
    <p>The Alder Street Library, which opened in 1986, is undergoing an accessibility renovation. Project architect Jordan Lee, whose firm won the public bid, presented the revised plan on May 14. Library director Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan on May 10, chaired the public meeting.</p>
    <p>The plan lists ten changes, four of which the board approved on May 14. Five community advisers, all of whom attended both evening sessions, supported those four changes. The eastern reading room, which seats 48, will reopen on September 9. The archive rooms that contain rare materials will remain closed through October; other archive rooms will reopen in September.</p>
    <p>Northline Construction, whose bid includes temporary ramps, will begin work on August 5. The board moved the public reopening from September 2 to September 9, which gives the finishing team one more week. The west entrance will remain closed during construction, which means visitors must use the east entrance.</p>
    <p>A neighborhood newsletter alleged that a late design review caused the schedule change. The official project file says the review took longer than forecast, but it does not establish that review as the only cause. A responsible summary attributes the allegation instead of embedding it as an undisputed parenthetical fact about Jordan.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the library date, architect association, formal review relationship, approved quantity, adviser scope, room subgroup, whole-clause schedule consequence, and evidence boundary.">
    <h3>Evidence check: noun comment, set, consequence, or identifying clue?</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The library opened in 1986; that date is additional information about the already identified Alder Street Library." data-hint="The full library name identifies the building before the opening-date comment." data-fix="The library opened in 1986, and the clause does not identify which library."><p class="quiz-question">1. What does the first non-defining clause contribute?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The library opened in 1986; that date is additional information about the already identified Alder Street Library.">The library opened in 1986; that date is additional information about the already identified Alder Street Library.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It selects one unnamed library from a list by using an unpunctuated clause.">It selects one unnamed library from a list by using an unpunctuated clause.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It says 1986 is renovating the library.">It says 1986 is renovating the library.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Jordan Lee’s firm won the public bid." data-hint="Whose links Jordan to the associated noun firm." data-fix="Jordan Lee’s firm won the public bid."><p class="quiz-question">2. What association does the clause about Jordan express?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Jordan Lee’s firm won the public bid.">Jordan Lee’s firm won the public bid.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Jordan Lee personally is the public bid.">Jordan Lee personally is the public bid.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every firm named Jordan won every bid.">Every firm named Jordan won every bid.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan on May 10, chaired the public meeting." data-hint="Use formal with whom for the person Jordan reviewed the plan with." data-fix="Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan on May 10, chaired the public meeting."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence preserves the formal review relationship?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan on May 10, chaired the public meeting.">Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan on May 10, chaired the public meeting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with who Jordan reviewed the plan with, chaired the meeting.">Dana Ruiz, with who Jordan reviewed the plan with, chaired the meeting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, that Jordan reviewed the plan, chaired the meeting.">Dana Ruiz, that Jordan reviewed the plan, chaired the meeting.</button></div></div>
