  <h2>Notice and repair the broken information structure</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="that" data-hint="A standard non-defining clause after an identified name cannot use that." data-fix="Jordan Lee, who presented the plan, answered questions." data-why="Use who for the person subject and pair commas around the inserted clause." data-success-message="Correct. Who restores the person reference while paired punctuation marks the parenthetical comment.">
    <h3>Repair 1: replace <span class="ex">that</span></h3><p>Tap the unavailable relative word.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="jordan">Jordan Lee,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="that">that</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="presented">presented the plan,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="answered">answered questions.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="i read" data-hint="An object relative can be omitted in a defining clause, but not in a non-defining clause." data-fix="The final report, which I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates." data-why="Which represents the report as object of read and must remain inside the parenthetical clause." data-success-message="Correct. Restoring which makes the object role and the opening boundary explicit.">
    <h3>Repair 2: restore the object relative</h3><p>Tap the phrase where the missing relative word belongs.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="report">The final report,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i read">I read</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="yesterday">yesterday,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="includes">includes the cost estimates.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="it" data-hint="Which already represents the final report as object of read." data-fix="The final report, which I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates." data-why="Do not repeat the represented object with it inside the relative clause." data-success-message="Correct. Removing it leaves one represented object and a complete main sentence.">
    <h3>Repair 3: remove the repeated object</h3><p>Tap the extra pronoun.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="report">The final report,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="which">which</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="read">I read</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it">it</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="yesterday">yesterday, includes the estimates.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="whose late review caused the delay" data-hint="The newsletter alleges this cause, but the official file does not establish it." data-fix="A newsletter alleged that a late design review caused the delay, but the project file does not establish that cause." data-why="A parenthetical clause backgrounds the cause as an assertion about Jordan; an attributed main clause preserves the unresolved evidence status." data-success-message="Correct. The revision attributes the causal allegation and prevents punctuation from presenting it as established fact.">
