  <h2>Practice information design without exposing private details</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to identify a real family member, coworker, employer, client, medical provider, immigration case, legal dispute, accessibility need, address, private organization, or disputed incident. Use Alder Street, public information with reliable sourcing, or tutor-created fictional profiles. The lesson tests information status and reference, not personal disclosure.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Scope switch:</b> Invent six candidates, two of whom have one relevant skill. Give a defining sentence that selects the two. Then establish a selected group whose members all share another feature and add that feature parenthetically.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register switch:</b> Describe one fictional professional first with <span class="ex">who I spoke with</span> and then with <span class="ex">with whom I spoke</span>. Keep the relationship constant and explain which channel suits each version.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Quantity report:</b> Introduce a set of people and a set of proposals. Add <span class="ex">all of whom</span>, <span class="ex">two of whom</span>, <span class="ex">three of which</span>, or <span class="ex">none of which</span> with exact fictional counts.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Attachment edit:</b> Create an intentionally unclear <span class="ex">which</span> sentence. Rewrite it once as a noun comment and once as a whole-proposition comment.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Source check:</b> Turn one unsupported parenthetical claim into an attributed main clause with a clear evidence limit.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second layered project briefing</h3>
    <p>Use Alder Street or another tutor-supplied fictional project. Begin with an already identified project, person, place, and date. Add one subject <span class="ex">who</span> clause, one object <span class="ex">which</span> clause, one <span class="ex">whose + noun</span> clause, and one <span class="ex">where</span> or <span class="ex">when</span> clause. Contrast one defining subgroup with one non-defining whole-group comment. Use one <span class="ex">of whom/of which</span> quantity, one formal fronted preposition or conversational stranded preposition, and one unambiguous whole-clause <span class="ex">which</span>. Mark the parenthetical thought groups naturally. When the editor challenges an inserted claim, identify its source, move it into a main clause, or remove it.</p>
    <p><b>Success criteria:</b> Can the listener recover every referent before each side comment, distinguish selected subgroup from identified whole, locate the relative word’s role, hear the parenthetical boundaries, recover the exact quantity and preposition relationship, identify the source of a whole-clause consequence, and separate supported background information from disputed claims?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved set scope, a required object relative, formal preposition placement, exact quantity, whole-clause consequence, and responsible attribution.">
    <h3>Final check: defend the information structure</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The advisers who attended both sessions supported the plan; only that subgroup is identified." data-hint="The context includes other advisers, so the unpunctuated clause selects the attendees." data-fix="The advisers who attended both sessions supported the plan."><p class="quiz-question">1. A larger adviser group existed, but only session attendees supported the plan. Which sentence preserves that subgroup meaning?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The advisers who attended both sessions supported the plan; only that subgroup is identified.">The advisers who attended both sessions supported the plan; only that subgroup is identified.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The advisers, who attended both sessions, supported the plan; the commas select only the attendees from the larger group.">The advisers, who attended both sessions, supported the plan; the commas select only the attendees from the larger group.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The advisers, that attended both sessions supported the plan.">The advisers, that attended both sessions supported the plan.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The final report, which I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates." data-hint="The report is already identified, and object which cannot be omitted in the parenthetical clause." data-fix="The final report, which I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence has a complete non-defining object relative?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final report, which I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates.">The final report, which I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final report, I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates.">The final report, I read yesterday, includes the cost estimates.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final report, which I read it yesterday, includes the cost estimates.">The final report, which I read it yesterday, includes the cost estimates.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan, chaired the meeting." data-hint="Formal fronting requires with before object whom, with no repeated final preposition." data-fix="Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan, chaired the meeting."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which formal sentence controls the preposition pattern?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan, chaired the meeting.">Dana Ruiz, with whom Jordan reviewed the plan, chaired the meeting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, with who Jordan reviewed the plan with, chaired the meeting.">Dana Ruiz, with who Jordan reviewed the plan with, chaired the meeting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana Ruiz, that Jordan reviewed the plan with, chaired the meeting.">Dana Ruiz, that Jordan reviewed the plan with, chaired the meeting.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The plan lists ten changes, four of which were approved." data-hint="The set contains things, and exactly four of ten received approval." data-fix="The plan lists ten changes, four of which were approved."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence reports the exact approved share?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The plan lists ten changes, four of which were approved.">The plan lists ten changes, four of which were approved.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The plan lists ten changes, four of whom were approved.">The plan lists ten changes, four of whom were approved.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The plan lists ten changes, which means all ten were approved.">The plan lists ten changes, which means all ten were approved.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the team one more week." data-hint="The extra week follows from the entire scheduling change." data-fix="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the team one more week."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence gives <span class="ex">which</span> an unambiguous whole-clause source?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The opening moved to September 9, which gave the team one more week.">The opening moved to September 9, which gave the team one more week.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete.">The team discussed the budget in May, which was incomplete.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The opening moved to September 9, that gave the team one more week.">The opening moved to September 9, that gave the team one more week.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A newsletter alleged that the late review caused the delay, but the official file does not establish that cause." data-hint="Attribute the claim and keep the documentary limit in main clauses." data-fix="A newsletter alleged that the late review caused the delay, but the official file does not establish that cause."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which sentence reports an unresolved cause responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A newsletter alleged that the late review caused the delay, but the official file does not establish that cause.">A newsletter alleged that the late review caused the delay, but the official file does not establish that cause.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Jordan, whose late review caused the delay, is fully responsible, although the file does not establish that cause.">Jordan, whose late review caused the delay, is fully responsible, although the file does not establish that cause.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The delay, which proves the allegation, requires no attribution.">The delay, which proves the allegation, requires no attribution.</button></div></div>
