    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">The listener can identify the referent because...</span> <span class="ex">The clause selects / separately asserts...</span> <span class="ex">The relative expression fills the role of...</span> <span class="ex">The main frame is...</span> <span class="ex">The exact set quantity is...</span> <span class="ex">The preposition belongs...</span> <span class="ex">Whole-clause which refers to...</span> <span class="ex">The source supports...</span> <span class="ex">The source does not establish...</span></p>
    <p>Then take one sentence from your briefing. Remove the inserted clause and state what identity remains and what assertion disappears. Add the clause again, say it as a parenthetical thought group, and check whether its source and attachment remain clear.</p>
